---
title: Invariants
description: A compiler and auto-regressive runtime for better LLM structured outputs.
date: 2026-08-18
href: https://github.com/ujaandas/invariants
---
**invariants** moves formal semantic verification directly into the token generation loop in C++. By validating partial generation state against schema invariants at each step, illegal tokens are pruned before they are ever sampled.

In essence, it is a compiler and inference-time verification engine designed to enforce deterministic, context-sensitive constraints during autoregressive LLM generation.

- **Custom DSL:** A schema definition language for declaring cross-field rules, dynamic ranges, and operational invariants.
- **Compiler pipeline:** Uses multi-stage tree walks and targeted codegen passes to turn schema constraints into fast evaluation routines for the sampler.
- **Runtime integration:** Evaluates constraints during the forward pass with minimal per-token overhead.
